oadways, as well as flash flood prone burn scars, washes,\nslot canyons, and arroyos. Early estimates predict an area of 1 to 2\ninches of new rainfall for portions of southeast UT and southwest CO.\n\nThis is a preliminary forecast that hinges on slight shifts in a\nstrong moisture plume impacting the region. It also attempts to\ncapture the most statistically likely outcome, despite stronger and\nweaker outlier predictions. Outdoor enthusiasts, motorists, and\nresidents of recent flood impacted areas are encouraged to remain\nabreast of the developing forecast in the coming days.","ends":"2026-10-30T15:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Dolores, CO; La Plata, CO; Montezuma, CO; San Miguel, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8fb5d34f2d13ed8ac1ea289950d1e46b096a7bdd.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8fb5d34f2d13ed8ac1ea289950d1e46b096a7bdd.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-29T17:13:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 291713 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1113 AM MDT Thu Oct 29 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Mild fall conditions continue today. - Precipitation chances return Friday with light rain at the lower elevations and flurries above 10,000 ft. - Deeper moisture arrives Saturday night and will increase the chances for impactful precipitation for southwe","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-29T18:40:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-301000- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1239 PM MDT Thu Oct 29 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?s